preConditionHook:
// Daily loss limit, for intraday series: off for the rest of the calendar
// day once the day's equity change falls below -X. MonthlyProfitTarget is the reference for the shape, statement for
// statement: equity = NetProfit + OpenPositionProfit (close-marked, net of the
// entry side's costs), snapshotted as the PRIOR bar's equity on the first bar
// of each new day. PrevPeriod/PrevEquity mirror the twin's
// CurrentPeriod[1]/CurrentEquity[1] -- an EL variable's own history, 0 before
// the strategy's first evaluated bar -- advanced in endOfFileHook so the value
// read here is always the previous bar's.
//
// PERIOD: the bar's wall-clock closing date, the standing session model
// (MaxTradesPerSession; EL_Date_Probe.txt). day_of() serial in C++, EL's
// YYYMMDD Date in the twin -- different encodings, but only inequality is
// tested. @HO's evening bars 1900-2300 carry the prior calendar date, so
// the 'day' there is the calendar day, not the 18:00 session. On a daily
// series every bar is a new day and this is a one-bar loss stop.
//
// LATCH CHECK: once the day's loss passes X the Switch forces flat and blocks entries, so
// equity stops moving; the next day boundary re-snapshots the start
// equity, the difference returns to 0, and trading resumes. It cannot disable
// the strategy for good. Direction-agnostic: both sides are identical text.
CurrentEquity = ctx.NetProfit() + ctx.OpenPositionProfit();
CurrentPeriod = day_of(ctx.Time(0));
if (el_ne((double)CurrentPeriod, (double)PrevPeriod)) {
    DayStartEquity = PrevEquity;
}
